  "appeal_start_date": "14/07/2026",
  "cil_liability": true,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The applicant has applied for the prior approval of the Local Planning Authority as required by paragraph B of Class A of Part 20 of Schedule 2 of the General Permitted Development Order, which is for development consisting of works for the construction of up to two additional storeys of new dwellinghouses immediately above the existing topmost residential storey on a building which is a purpose-built, detached block of flats. Block A and B (flats 1-6 and 7-12) are semi-detached as they share an internal party wall and are accessed via separate entrances, therefore this proposal fails to meet the criteria as set out in Class A of Part 20 of Schedule 2 of the General Permitted Development Order.",
    "The proposed development, by reason of the increased scale and massing, would result in an imposing and dominant development which would fail to enhance the character and appearance of the existing buildings and surrounding area. The proposed buildings would significantly exceed the prevailing heights of existing buildings within the vicinity and create an incongruous form of development that fails to adequately reflect its location. The proposed development would therefore result in harm to the character and appearance of the surrounding area contrary to Policies D3 and D4 of the London Plan and Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.\r",
    "The proposed development by reason of the absence of a completed S106 legal agreement to secure the prohibition of the future occupiers from obtaining residents or visitor car parking permits at this location, would result in overspill car parking to the detriment of the safe and efficient operation of the public highway and would be contrary to sub-paragraph A.2(1)(a) of schedule 2, Part 20, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 2015 (as amended) and Policy 37 of the Sutton Local Plan (2018).",
    "The proposal by reason of the additional stories and new windows to Block A, B and E it would result in perceived and actual overlooking and loss of privacy to the residential occupiers of the neighbouring properties in Oakhill Road to the north and Burnell Road to the south of the site and would fail to comply with condition A.2.(1)(g) of Schedule 2, Part 20, Class A of The Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015(as amended) and Policy D3 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan (2018).\r"
  ],
